provides vacation services. JetBlue Airways Corporation was incorporated in 1998 and is based in Long Island City, New York.","ceo_bio":"Ms. Joanna L. Geraghty | CEO & Director | Age 52 | Compensation: $1.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 19K people. Revenue per employee of $459K ranks in the above the sector median among Industrials peers, improving at 6%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $2K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["JetBlue Airways Corporation is a small-cap industrials business with a $1.4B market cap on $9.1B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -0% over the past three years and +4% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at -4% against a 8% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $1.2B of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, debt is heavy at 17.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and leverage like that is what turns a bad year into a permanent loss, and thin -0.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Net dilution runs at 3.8% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 11% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.5) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (32.9% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Operating margins 13% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Carries a 734% premium to sector median EV/EBITDA","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":7.342586989409984},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (79% sell ratio) over the past year","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.214},{"text":"Value-trap profile (score 60/100): leveraged balance sheet under pressure; roic below cost of capital \u2014 cheapness may reflect deterioration, not mispricing","sev":"amber","cat":"value_trap"},{"text":"Tariff and trade-policy exposure \u2014 industrial exporters sit squarely in the crosshairs of protectionist policy, and retaliatory tariffs can close markets without warning.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"news_headlines":[{"title":"JetBlue's Defiant CFO to Employees: 'Not Considering Bankruptcy'","source":"bloomberg.com","link":"https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-11-06/jetblue-s-defiant-cfo-to-employees-not-considering-bankruptcy","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793999756.518,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.226,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":["leadership"]},{"title":"Major US Airline Slaps Holiday Travelers With a New $70 Baggage Fee","source":"aol.com","link":"https://www.aol.com/articles/major-us-airline-slaps-holiday-143300000.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793986954.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.402,"tier":2,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Delta, United, And JetBlue Officially Ordered To E